# Run requests one by one in Visual Studio / VS Code (REST Client) / Rider.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5193

### Public: health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### Public: log in as the seeded demo user. Copy "token" from the response into @token below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "demo", "password": "Demo1234!" }

###
@token = paste-token-here

### Protected: without a token this returns 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks

### Protected: current user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List tasks (optionally ?status=Todo|InProgress|Done)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a task
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Try the API", "description": "From the .http file", "status": "Todo", "dueDate": null }

### Change the status of several tasks at once (what the board does when you drag a card).
### Paste two "id" values from "List tasks" above. All or nothing: an unknown id returns 404 and nothing changes.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ids": ["paste-task-id-1", "paste-task-id-2"], "status": "Done" }

### Validation error (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "", "dueDate": "2000-01-01" }
